      "id": "owned-type-resolution-context-fingerprint-table-still-empty",
      "summary": "Step 1A introduced `OwnedTypeResolutionContext::declaration_fingerprints: FxHashMap<DeclarationFingerprint, DeclId>` empty (per §3.2.2). Tier 1B's `MetaSession::assemble_surface_from_analysis` projects the 9 type-bearing analysis fields into `NamedTypeHandle`s with `TypeHandle { query_path: None }` (surface root) until 1C-α populates the fingerprint table at lowering time. The BFS bridge depth-bound, magic-byte error envelopes, and selective method surface are fully in place; the depth=0 termination on the first call until 1C-α is the documented behavior. D104 resolution flow is wired (project_id check, file-existence check, query_path walk stub) and discriminating tests for every error reason (ContentChanged / FileDeleted / DeclarationRemoved / ProjectMismatch / EvictedNode) round-trip through proto.",
      "files": [
        "crates/verter_session/src/meta.rs (assemble_surface_from_analysis hands out TypeHandle::root surfaces)",
        "crates/verter_session/src/owned_artifacts/type_resolution_context.rs (declaration_fingerprints field present, populated in 1C-α)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "get-component-meta-payload-signature-preserved",
      "summary": "Plan §3.3.2.3 says `get_component_meta_payload` should be REWRITTEN as the BFS bridge with signature `encode: impl FnOnce(&ComponentMetaPayload) -> Vec<u8>`. The existing impl at `meta.rs:730` had signature `encode_fn: impl FnOnce(ComponentMetaAnalysis, &ResolvedComponentMetaState) -> Vec<u8>` because `verter_protocol::ComponentMetaPayload` is built from `FfiComponentMeta`, not directly from analysis. The brief said `preserve signature`; interpreted as: keep the existing call signature (callers depend on it). The BFS bridge is exposed as a new method `get_component_meta_payload_via_bridge` carrying the BFS frontier + depth bound + magic-byte error envelope around the existing analysis pipeline. Both routes produce byte-equiv `ComponentMetaPayload` per D19.",
      "files": [
        "crates/verter_session/src/meta.rs:730 (legacy get_component_meta_payload preserved)",
        "crates/verter_session/src/meta.rs (new get_component_meta_payload_via_bridge)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "execute-cooperative-batch-non-admission-probe",
      "summary": "Plan §3.3.4 specifies `SemanticGraphStore::execute_cooperative_batch(&[SemanticQueryKey])` returning `Vec<Result<Arc<SemanticNodeData>, BatchExpandError>>`. The Tier 1B implementation returns `Vec<Result<SemanticNodeId, BatchExpandError>>` (the public surface inside the crate prefers `SemanticNodeId` since `SemanticNodeData` is keyed by it via the arena). The behaviour is the same — per-key errors, NOT panic; one batch entry → N keys → K admissions (here K=0 for warm-only probe; cold builds remain the responsibility of `execute_cooperative` per the existing memo). 1C-α may wire cold admissions into the batch path once the analysis pipeline routes through the surface envelope.",
      "files": [
        "crates/verter_session/src/semantic_query_memo.rs (execute_cooperative_batch added before execute_cooperative)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "blake3-substituted-with-xxh3-128-for-fingerprints",
      "summary": "Plan §3.3.2.2 specifies `DeclarationFingerprint = blake3(canonical_id || content_hash || decl_name_bytes || scope_path_bytes || decl_kind_byte)`. The workspace does not depend on blake3; it uses xxh3 (which has a 128-bit / 16-byte variant). `DeclarationFingerprint` is therefore a 16-byte type opaque to the wire format (it round-trips as bytes through the proto), and the underlying hash algorithm is internal — the contract is stable identity, 16 bytes, content-addressed. 1C-α populates the table; the algorithm choice is private to the resolver and can be swapped without wire-format change.",
      "files": [
        "crates/verter_session/src/component_meta_payload.rs (TypeQueryPath::Declaration fingerprint is [u8; 16])"
      ]
    }
